From ef654c9122eef535eede947261509b8e188479be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Lamb <paul@paulscode.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 08:17:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] lightningd: re-arm the funding depth watch across a
 restart

A channel waiting for its funding to reach minimum_depth is told about each
new block by a depth watch, and that watch is registered when we first see
the funding output in a block. We do not register it again at startup. We
re-register the scriptpubkey watch that finds the funding, but that only
fires on blocks we process, and at startup we rescan fifteen of them.

So a channel whose funding confirmed more than a rescan ago, and which is
still short of its depth, comes back up watching for something it has already
seen and waits for a callback that never arrives.

Today this needs a minimum_depth larger than an operator would usually set,
which is why it has not bitten. The next commit makes a channel wait
thousands of blocks, and a restart in that window is not unlikely but
expected, so fix the general case first.

The scid is in the database, and its block height is the height the watch
wants. watch_blockdepth already refuses to add a watch identical to one it
holds, so re-arming here costs nothing when the rescan does reach the funding
block and finds it the usual way.
---
 lightningd/peer_control.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lightningd/peer_control.c b/lightningd/peer_control.c
index 13c5137a4..5344863b4 100644
--- a/lightningd/peer_control.c
+++ b/lightningd/peer_control.c
@@ -2965,6 +2965,21 @@ static void setup_peer(struct peer *peer)
 
 		/* Normal cases where we watch funding */
 		case CHANNELD_AWAITING_LOCKIN:
+			/* If the funding confirmed before we last stopped we
+			 * will not be told about it again: the scriptpubkey
+			 * watch only fires on blocks we process, and we
+			 * rescan a handful of them at startup. Pick the depth
+			 * watch back up from the scid we already stored, or
+			 * we will wait for a callback that never comes.
+			 *
+			 * Harmless if the rescan does reach the funding
+			 * block: watch_blockdepth ignores a watch it already
+			 * holds. */
+			if (channel->scid)
+				channel_watch_depth(ld,
+						    short_channel_id_blocknum(*channel->scid),
+						    channel);
+			/* Fall thru */
 		case CHANNELD_NORMAL:
 		case CHANNELD_SHUTTING_DOWN:
 		case CLOSINGD_SIGEXCHANGE:
